1
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:56,530
Sam, would you come in, please? Sam

2
00:00:56,530 --> 00:01:01,530
You sound like something's bothering you, Susan.

3
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:04,530
The sketches for the cover of the new doll book?

4
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,530
That's not it.

5
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:07,530
Please sit down.

6
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:08,530
Sure.

7
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:16,530
I need your advice on a personsal matter,

8
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:17,530
but it's not about me.

9
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:20,530
You need my advice on a personal matter,

10
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:22,530
and it's not about you.

11
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:25,530
It's about my grandfather.

12
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:27,530
What's the problem?

13
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:30,530
It won't sound like a big deal,

14
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:31,530
but it is.

15
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:33,530
I had dinner with him Saturday,

16
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:35,530
and he's very unhappy about not working.

17
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:38,530
I thought he was retired

18
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:39,530
and pleased to be living with the family.

19
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:41,530
He is,

20
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:44,530
but there's so much energy and talent in the man,

21
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:45,530
and he doesn't get to use it.

22
00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:46,530
But what can I do?

23
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:48,530
What kind of advice are you looking for?

24
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:50,530
Simply this.

25
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:53,530
John Marchetta runs this company. John Marchetta

26
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,530
He founded this company.

27
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:55,530
Right.

28
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:59,530
John Marchetta gave me my start here six years ago,

29
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:02,530
When I first graduated from college.

30
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:05,530
He gave me the chance to use my talents

31
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:07,530
and made me feel more confident.

32
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:10,530
Right.

33
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:12,530
Maybe he can do the same thing for your grandfather.

34
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:16,530
Or at least give him some advice.

35
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:17,530
Right.

36
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:19,530
Then I've solved your problem.

37
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:23,530
I can always depend on you, Sam.

38
00:02:23,530 --> 00:02:25,530
I'm glad to help.

39
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:28,530
Shall I call Mr. Marchetta for you?

40
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:31,530
No, no. I'll do that.

41
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:33,530
Thanks.

42
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:40,530
Now, how's the Stewart family?

43
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:42,530
Fine, thank you, Mr. Mrarchetta.

44
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:45,530
Except for my grandfather.

45
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:47,530
What's wrong, Susan?

46
00:02:47,530 --> 00:02:49,530
What's wrong with him?

47
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:51,530
He needs to work.

48
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:57,530
In fact, that is the reason why I'm here to see you.

49
00:02:57,530 --> 00:03:01,530
I know you're building a new factory,

50
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:04,530
and I thought ... maybe ...

51
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:07,530
my grandfather is

52
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:09,530
so experienced in the construction trade,

53
00:03:09,530 --> 00:03:12,530
he could be so valuable.

54
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:15,530
Tell him to come and see me

55
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:18,530
at ten o'clock tomorrow morning.

56
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:20,530
I have an idea that may solve the problem for him

57
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:22,530
and help a lot of other people.

58
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:23,530
Really, Mr. Marchetta?

59
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:25,530
Can I tell him that?

60
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:26,530
Sure can.

61
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:27,530
Ten o'clock in the morning. Here.

62
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:30,530
Oh, thank you!
